  "text": "118. The Supreme Court used the 'Mischief Rule' of interpretation to analyze the definition of\n\"manufacturing process\" by comparing the Factories Act, 1948, with its predecessor.\nWhat was the critical difference noted in the 1948 Act's definition (Section 2(k))\ncompared to the 1934 Act's definition (Section 2(g))?\n(A) The 1948 Act introduced the concept of \"power\" being used in the process.\n(B) The 1948 Act included the words 'washing, cleaning', which were absent in the\n1934 Act.\n(C) The 1948 Act removed the exemption for mobile units of the armed forces.\n(D) The 1948 Act lowered the minimum age of employment for children.",
